Z||000031||stimpy||02-07-2001||01:01 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MR2 and FIERO owner:<BR><B>that is why i joined the fiero forum i wanted to learn more about fieros. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hell of a way to introduce yourself. Did you get that from the Carnegie course? Kinda like showing up at a Black History Month event in a white hood cuz you want to learn about the civil rights struggle. My suggestion? Back up, re-register, and come back correct. There is enough love for everyone if you leave the dis at home.<P>Now, where is Pearl Blue Soul when you need him?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000032||Neverfinished||02-07-2001||01:09 AM||||Not to start a war here guys but i"m sticking up for the MR2 just a little bit. True a 4 banger MR2 is a gutless little ****  box and my 2.5 can beat them , but step into a supercharged MR2 (1989) and kiss your V-6 fiero goodbye. Try 130 HP in a car weighing hundreds of pounds lighter than our domestics. I don't believe in just driving domestic because I'm not japanese. Anyone who has the idea that only american cars are worth driving needs their head checked. I have smoked many v-6 fieros in imports (accords...). I love my fiero and will always have one in my garage but just get used to the high reving engines because they are coming to a GM near you. And already have. Also anyone who refers to japanese car lovers as ricers and japs need their head checked. I have many japanese friends and I have to see them put up with NRA members and assholes like you guys. I may be a new member but I''ve been keeping track on this forum for a long time and am getting disgusted with all the bitter arguing and racism . I am only speaking to the minority of a@@holes on here as 99% of you guys have been very very usefull! anyone else who feels the same way I do pleez don't let racism and hillbilly crap keep clogging up the forum!<P><BR>Thanks <BR>Vince(Neverfinished)||||reg||13
Z||000033||Oreif||02-07-2001||01:30 AM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Neverfinished:<BR><B>step into a supercharged MR2 (1989) and kiss your V-6 fiero goodbye. Try 130 HP in a car weighing hundreds of pounds lighter than our domestics. Vince(Neverfinished)</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Vince, Just a some True Facts. My 1986 SE weighs Approx. 2680lbs with a 140hp/134 torque 2.8L V-6. Per Toyota's Historical site, a 1989 MR2 supercharged weighs 2728 (2816 for T-top version) and is rated at 132HP/68 torque. A 4-cyl has inherently less torque than a V-6. So my Fiero weighs 48 pounds less and has 8HP more!<P>If you are going to give specs, please verify your sources. With the internet, it is very easy to verify a cars stock specs.<BR>1989 MR2 specs listed at link below.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.j-garage.com/311013.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.j-garage.com/311013.htm</A> <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 02-07-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000034||Neverfinished||02-07-2001||02:05 AM||||thank you oreif for your know how. Too bad specs don't mean sheet in the real world. True not everyone who owns a v-6 knows how to drive but I've wasted three v-6's in a super mr2 and they are smokin fast. I would however choose a v-6 fiero any day.<BR>P.S. I'm white for all you a@@holes who think i'm a jap or a ricer. I'm just glad I'm just not stuck in the past 60's - 80's muscle car era. Gas burning poor handling "american pride" mobiles.<BR>thanks guys||||reg||1
Z||000035||Neverfinished||02-07-2001||02:09 AM||||Plus I had my info all wrong. It was a 86 supercharged T-Tops white which produced 145 hp and weighed alot less than a v-6 fiero. sorry oreif. Didn't mean to mix up my info. You are right about the 89's.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000036||Sleeper||02-07-2001||02:39 AM||||boy, this guy suckered you all into a sh*ttalkin' contest, you should have ignored his post...somebody said this forum is great, well it is, but sh*t like this f*cks it up.<P>------------------<BR>85 GT<BR>17" Racing Hart C5 wheels, Kumho Ecsta Supra 712 tires, Intrax lowering spring, KYB shocks, KYB-GR2 struts, Chris West's Strut Tower Bar, Accel Super Coil, Accel Wires, K&N filter and Optima Battery.||||reg||1
Z||000037||Neverfinished||02-07-2001||02:46 AM||||I never got suckered in to this guys post. I just believe that imports don't get the respect they deserve thats all. every member could argue all day and night about cars, and never win. I consider this topic over and would just like to ask all members of the forum to ease up on the racial crap. It really gives the forum a bad image.||||reg||1
Z||000038||Oreif||02-07-2001||03:02 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Neverfinished:<BR><B>Plus I had my info all wrong. It was a 86 supercharged T-Tops white which produced 145 hp and weighed alot less than a v-6 fiero. sorry oreif. Didn't mean to mix up my info. You are right about the 89's.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>OK an 86 Supercharged MR2 is 285 pounds lighter, HP is only 125 and torque is only 41. (You need to convert from metric to english) See below: <A HREF="http://www.j-garage.com/311012.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.j-garage.com/311012.htm</A> <P>Why do people think MR2's are better? They are about the same as Fiero's in Power to weight ratio's, They are both 2-seaters, and it only took Pontiac 1 year to come up with a GT version where Toyota had to wait until 86 to add some HP and didn't change to an aerodynamic body style until 1989! Like you say, specs don't mean "sheet" in the real world. Since EVERY automobile manufacturer underrates the cars, what makes you think GM is any different than Toyota.<BR>Your comment on "poor handling" is incorrect also. A stock Fiero has out handled EVERY stock MR2. This is proven by Road and Track in 1986 and again in 1988. Car and Driver tested a 1988 Fiero Formula against an 89 MR2 and the Fiero out handled the MR2! MotorTrend Tested an 85 Fiero GT against an 85 MR2 and it smoked the MR2 in all catagories! Yes there are many cars on the road today both Fiero and MR2 that have upgrades that make them better than stock. <BR>Right now there are Forums for both cars and a lot of these arguements could be settled on both forums if people would just spend some time and review facts. <P>I'll get off the soap box now.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000039||Sleeper||02-07-2001||03:09 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Neverfinished:<BR><B>I just believe that imports don't get the respect they deserve thats all... would just like to ask all members of the forum to ease up on the racial crap. It really gives the forum a bad image.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>true dat, true dat, i feel the same way, most of my friends have imports, i respect them alot and i know their potential(import cars). but dude, you're sticking up for imports on the wrong forum, most of the ppl here consider them ricers and thats that.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000040||Neverfinished||02-07-2001||03:17 AM||||ok oreif, Instead of picking apart my posts for some minute little detail that you obviously misread. I was stating that 60's -80 era cars were poor handling cars. I own a fiero ws6 and I know how they handle and i know what has been written on them. I have wasted every car on twisty roads i have raced. thank you once again for your extensive knowledge base but read a little better before you try to make me look like an idiot. I would never own an mr2 and I love my fiero. just don't dis imports because most of you old guys haven't been in nice imports. (not all of the members).<BR>Thank you||||reg||1
