Z||000065||Will||02-07-2001||04:32 PM||||Why is this in TD&Q?<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B> OK an 86 Supercharged MR2 is 285 pounds lighter, HP is only 125 and torque is only 41. (You need to convert from metric to english) See below: <A HREF="http://www.j-garage.com/311012.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.j-garage.com/311012.htm</A> <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>While you don't NEED to convert from metric to english, when you do convert, you do need to do it correctly. To go from kgm to ftlb you need to multiply by 2.2 (lb/kg), then multiply by 3.28 (ft/m). The page you sited states that the supercharged MR2 has 137 ftlbs.<P>You bloody thin skinned people are worse than the ACLU.<BR>That's my take on the racism issue.<BR>Why was it even brought up? With a few notable exceptions (like Lisa &lt;wolf whistle&gt;  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ) we are just faceless typists. I think ones who are constantly crying "Racism! Racism!" at everything they hear are the most racist themselves.||||reg||1
