Z||000067||gabriel||02-07-2001||06:06 PM||||Hey JK !<P>  What you didn't get from my post is that the remarks may be rude & insensitive (to you) But they are NOT racist !!!<P>  Why don't you leave the frozen tundra of Ole Canada for a few, and come down here to S. Florida?  We'll drive our Fieros, & I'll show you around - visit Disney - & introduce you to some REAL racists -  the KKK chapters herebouts!<P>  Placing me  & others in that catagory because a remark offends your heritage is an insult to me personally.  - This is my last post here - so do go ahead & have the last word, but remember - you might be sounding  like a self aggrandizing person with a self inflated ego.<BR> Just rappin to ya, dude.  Freedom of speech isn't just a bunch of words here, it's an engrained concept & BTW?  I'm really not trying to offend you - perhaps I have, perhaps I have - you now have my apologies - lets start over & get down to the thing of it all ...  Fieros!!!!<BR>  (what a great forum!)||||reg||1
Z||000068||zeusrekning||02-07-2001||07:58 PM||||My dad is not asian.He is form calif. and was in the army. HE eats rice three meals a day. I asked if he was offended and he said no. So its ok. Keep calling them ricers. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>A guy i work with and my boss also, drive nissans, they call there cars rice and "the rice rocket.i don't see it as being offensive.Living down here in SC you here a lot about racism. I think battles need to be choosen.I am anti ricer. I prefer older american cars. If i owned a honda i'd be a ricer in a month. I mean full blown 2 foot wing,stickers and all. This is just my fault.Lot of aftermarket goodies. Think we need to keep this forum fiero related , mainly so we all get along.||||reg||1
