Z||000077||fierospeeder||02-08-2001||02:16 AM||||I hope im not a ricer because i own a honda nighthawk. aka motorcycle.  Something honda should stick with instead of building cars.<P>Id rather have a motorcycle engine on my bike instead of being built in my car.  <P>Typical motorcycle engine are able to rev to <BR>10,000 rpms and have several timing belts to turn their ohc.<P>As for "ricers", i dont see that many "orientals" driving them.  As a college student, i see many suburbian white kids that go to starbucks, who drink their bottled evian water, and own these so called "riced up cars".  They have their hat put on backwards, blasting their 1000 watt stereo system driving their "ricer" car, with the stickers all over it, and the coffee can exhaust which they had left over when starbucks was closed during those late nights.  The coffee at home was the only thing they had.<P>As for american cars being not very economic for the environment.  Thats very bias when 90% of the "yuppy" population is buying SUVs.  Honda plus the other japanese car makers are building SUVs for the market because everyone wants one.  Who cares if my SUV gets 15mpg, i want my 80cubic feet of interior space.<P>The only fair way to compare the mr2 to the fiero is by the same year.  You cant compare a 89, 95 etc.. mr2 to a 84 fiero when the technology of a car has changed over the years.  And the real way to say one car is better then another is by the written facts that magazines have put out.  Take the average of what "Car and Driver" and "Motor Trend" says about the mr2 compared to the fiero and you get your answer.  You cant drag race someone on the street and say Ya, all mr2s are faster because someone didn't feel like drag racing, their car is in bad shape, or they were cop scared.  I have dragraced people until the speed limit and i have let them win, because its not worth wasting gas or getting a 100 dollar ticket.<P>Another thing that hasn't come up, but someone might say is a jap car is a lot more dependible.  Until 60,000 miles has hit the odometer in a ricer vehicle, a mechanic will want 1000 bucks to change a timing belt. Must be fun repairing a ricer, but mostly everyone sells their ricer to get a brand new one. <P> No one can judge one car from another when they dont take care of their vehicle.  Id rather fix a 12 year old american car then a foreign car.  Parts are too expensive and harder to get.  Plus american cars are a lot easier to fix.  The people on horsepower tv was doing a upgrade on a ricer car and they went to a ricer track.  These guys hotrod american cars 99% of the time.  Then that one chubby guy says ya, that honda got 10 secs on the strip.  1/8 mile strip while the light buzz of the engine was going buy.  Ear plugs are not necessary.<P>while the mr2 guy gets a 500 dollar fiero, dont say its a piece of crap.  Any car will be if your getting it for that much money.<P>Cliff please forgive me<BR>i hope your on vacation so dont read this<P>||||reg||1
Z||000078||MR2 and FIERO owner||02-08-2001||10:55 AM||||WELL DAMM THATS THE TRUTH A SUPERCHARGED MR2 CAN GET DOWN WITH ALLMOST ANY CAR ON THE ROAD TODAY. I REMEMBER LAST SUMMER I KILLED A VIPER ON THE FREEWAY.DOING 154MPH.BUT I NEVER RACE OTHER MR2S OF FIEROS.BECAUSE I RESPECT THEM.BUT IF A FIERO EVER WANT TO RUMBLE WE CAN GO&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;<BR>                   <BR>                &gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;||||reg||1
Z||000079||AkursedX||02-08-2001||11:17 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MR2 and FIERO owner:<BR>[B]I REMEMBER LAST SUMMER I KILLED A VIPER ON THE FREEWAY.DOING 154MPH.[B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You know, I thought I could keep my mouth shut through this, but a VIPER??  Surrrree, you might as well just made it a McClaren F-1.  I'm sure we would believe that one too.<P>This is why have a bumper sticker on my winter car that says "Stupidity Should Be Painful"  It also adds 15 horsepower  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> j/k  <P>Ohhh, but as for this whole ricer/domestic fight, it's really getting old.  Who really cares who's car is better.  People are entitled to think whatever they want. I don't like any sort of car-bashing, for this exact reason, it gets way too out of hand, and nothing good ever comes of it.  <BR>Ok, I'll shut up now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
